FINAL ANSWER:
Troy Goode and Douglas Christopher Wilson own most of the surviving code. Troy owns about 40% and Douglas about 31%.

The default blame tool credits "Fiona Formatter" with 51% of the lines. That is wrong for your question. Fiona's only commit is `62628c0`, the 4-space and double-quote reformat. Blame attributes every line that commit touched to Fiona, even though the logic comes from earlier authors.

I re-ran `git blame` with that commit ignored (`--ignore-rev 62628c0 -w -M -C`) across all 18 tracked files. That gives about 2,000 surviving lines, split like this:

| Author | Lines | Share (approx.) | Last commit |
|---|---|---|---|
| Troy Goode | 810 | ~40% | 2026-04-10 |
| Douglas Christopher Wilson | 629 | ~31% | 2021-09-07 |
| Íñigo Marquínez Prado | 95 | ~5% | 2024-05-14 |
| Jon Church | 72 | ~4% | 2026-01-16 |
| Sebastian Beltran | 67 | ~3% | 2025-07-23 |
| Ulises Gascón | 52 | ~3% | 2026-01-22 |
| Ignacio Mangas | 44 | ~2% | 2025-12-01 |
| Everyone else | under 30 each | the rest | — |

The percentages use the older ~2,000-line total from the first tool run. I did not recompute it after ignoring the reformat, so they are approximate.

- **Core code:** In `lib/index.js`, Troy owns 159 of 238 lines and Douglas owns 22. Alejandro Caravaca Puchades has 12, Raymond Feng has 7, and max.laverse has 6.
- **Tests:** `test/test.js` is split almost evenly between Douglas (339 lines) and Troy (317).
- **Config, CI and docs:** These are spread across Douglas, Íñigo, Sebastian, Ulises, Ignacio, and Jon.

Every file is orphaned under the tool's rule. The tool counts an author as inactive if they have no commit since 2026-04-22. By that rule all the authors above are inactive.

- Troy's last commit was 2026-04-10, so they just missed the cutoff.
- Douglas's last commit was in 2021, so their lines have gone longest without their own touch.
- Fiona's formatting commit is the most recent of all, and that commit is also what makes the default numbers misleading.

